          }
        },
        {
          "id": "ctg-9",
          "type": "text",
          "data": {
            "html": "<p>In an oxidizing electric kiln, 1.5% red iron oxide fires a warm honey yellow. Starve the gas burners of oxygen at 980°C so carbon monoxide steals an oxygen atom—reducing Fe2O3 to FeO—and the same glaze melts into translucent jade.</p>",
            "variables": []
          },
          "style": {
            "padding": {
              "top": 0,
              "right": 40,
              "bottom": 28,
              "left": 40
            },
            "alignment": "left",
            "fontSize": 17,
            "lineHeight": 1.65,
            "color": "#1C1A17"
          }
        },
        {
